---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { fullSrc, IMAGES } from '../../lib/site';
import Pic from '../../components/Pic.astro';
import MotionClips from '../../components/MotionClips.astro';
import DataFlowDiagram from '../../components/DataFlowDiagram.astro';
import DaySequence from '../../components/DaySequence.astro';
import { stats, modules, stack, broke, differently, screenshots, shot } from '../../data/internal-dashboard';
---
<Base title="Case study: the Internal Dashboard" section="ai"
  description="How Cameron Kuey took Doodle Pirates Foundation’s all-in-one Internal Dashboard from concept to production in under two weeks with Claude Code and AI coding agents: 152 reviewed PRs, 1,218 tests.">
  <article>
    <div class="wrap">
      <header class="page-head wide">
        <ol class="crumbs eyebrow" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><li><a href="/ai-builds">AI Builds</a></li><li>Case study</li></ol>
        <h1>An all-in-one Internal Dashboard, <em>concept to production in under two weeks.</em></h1>
        <p class="lede">As product owner at Doodle Pirates Foundation, I designed and shipped one role-based platform for the whole team, built with Claude Code, Claude Design and AI coding agents, with a human reviewing every change.</p>
      </header>
    </div>

    <section style="padding-top:8px"><div class="wrap">
      <figure class="cs-vis cs-hero-vis">
        <span class="tag">Sample data</span>
        <Pic id={shot.myWork.id} alt={shot.myWork.alt} eager sizes="(max-width: 1280px) 100vw, 1200px" />
      </figure>
      <div class="stats cs-statbar">
        {stats.map((s) => <div class="stat"><b>{s.value}</b><span>{s.label}</span></div>)}
      </div>
      <p class="cs-note">The savings figure is my estimate of the separate tools and subscriptions this one platform replaces, per employee per year. It is not an audited number.</p>
    </div></section>

    <section class="cs-vspace"><div class="wrap cs-split">
      <div class="cs-text">
        <h2>The problem</h2>
        <p>Doodle Pirates Foundation is a nonprofit, and much of the team is neurodivergent. I built the dashboard partly to give each person one simple place that shows what to focus on each day.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cs-vis phones">
        <span class="tag">Sample data</span>
        <Pic id={shot.phoneFocus.id} alt={shot.phoneFocus.alt} sizes="240px" />
        <Pic id={shot.phoneOtis.id} alt={shot.phoneOtis.alt} sizes="240px" />
      </div>
    </div></section>

    <section class="cs-vspace"><div class="wrap cs-split rev">
      <div class="cs-text">
        <h2>What it does</h2>
        <p>One role-based platform for the whole team, replacing a stack of separate tools. By my estimate, it avoids <strong>$1,000+ per employee in annual software costs</strong>.</p>
        <ul class="taglist">{modules.map((m) => <li>{m}</li>)}</ul>
      </div>
      <figure class="cs-vis">
        <span class="tag">Sample data</span>
        <Pic id={shot.projects.id} alt={shot.projects.alt} sizes="(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 700px" />
      </figure>
    </div></section>

    <section class="cs-vspace"><div class="wrap cs-split">
      <div class="cs-text">
        <h2>Ask Otis</h2>
        <p>Ask Otis is a Claude-powered assistant built into the dashboard. Ask it to add a task, update one, or change a project or milestone, and it comes back with an editable card.</p>
        <p>Nothing changes until the person presses Approve, and the server checks their permissions again before saving.</p>
      </div>
      <MotionClips only={['ask-otis-approve-suggestion']} cols={1} />
    </div></section>

    <section class="cs-vspace"><div class="wrap cs-split rev">
      <div class="cs-text">
        <h2>From meetings to daily focus</h2>
        <p>The dashboard doesn’t read meeting notes. Action items go into the task list, added by people and by AI assistants we run outside the dashboard.</p>
        <p>Every weekday at 6:30 AM, the dashboard picks 3 to 5 tasks for each person’s daily focus, using AI with a short reason for each. If the AI is slow or down, a rule-based picker fills in.</p>
      </div>
      <figure class="cs-vis">
        <span class="tag">Sample data</span>
        <Pic id={shot.focusDeck.id} alt={shot.focusDeck.alt} sizes="(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 700px" />
      </figure>
    </div></section>

    <section class="cs-vspace"><div class="wrap">
      <div class="cs-split" style="margin-bottom:32px">
        <div class="cs-text">
          <h2>How data flows</h2>
          <p>Everyone signs in with their work Google account. Every write goes through the API, which checks permissions and then writes to Airtable, the source of truth. Docs are real Google Docs, and shifts and PTO go one way to Google Calendar. Ask Otis only suggests; a person approves first.</p>
        </div>
        <div></div>
      </div>
      <DataFlowDiagram />
    </div></section>

    <section class="cs-vspace"><div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head"><h2>A day in the dashboard</h2><p class="eyebrow">From meeting action items to a confirmed week</p></div>
      <div style="margin-top:28px"><DaySequence /></div>
    </div></section>

    <section class="cs-vspace"><div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head"><h2>See it in motion</h2><p class="eyebrow">Sample-data screen recordings</p></div>
      <div style="margin-top:28px"><MotionClips only={['opening-the-day', 'kiosk-clock-in']} /></div>
    </div></section>

    <section class="cs-vspace"><div class="wrap cs-split">
      <div class="cs-text">
        <h2>How it was built</h2>
        <p>I directed AI coding agents as product owner and reviewed their work: 152 pull requests, each one reviewed, backed by 1,218 automated tests.</p>
        <dl class="spec" style="grid-template-columns:1fr">
          {stack.map(([k, v]) => <div><dt>{k}</dt><dd>{v}</dd></div>)}
        </dl>
      </div>
      <div class="cs-vis pair">
        <span class="tag">Sample data</span>
        <figure><Pic id={shot.docs.id} alt={shot.docs.alt} sizes="(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 340px" /><figcaption>{shot.docs.label}</figcaption></figure>
        <figure><Pic id={shot.onboarding.id} alt={shot.onboarding.alt} sizes="(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 340px" /><figcaption>{shot.onboarding.label}</figcaption></figure>
      </div>
    </div></section>

    <section class="cs-vspace"><div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head"><h2>Screens</h2><p class="eyebrow">Sample data only</p></div>
      <div class="shots dash-shots" data-gallery>
        {screenshots.map((s) => (
          <figure class={`shot${s.phone ? ' is-phone' : ''}`}>
            <a class="shot-img" href={fullSrc(s.id)} data-lb data-w={IMAGES[s.id].w} data-h={IMAGES[s.id].h} data-cap={`${s.label} (sample data)`} aria-label={`View larger: ${s.alt}`}>
              <span class="tag">Sample data</span>
              <Pic id={s.id} alt={s.alt} sizes={s.phone ? '(max-width: 900px) 50vw, 260px' : '(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 560px'} />
            </a>
            <figcaption><b>{s.label}</b>{s.note && <span>{s.note}</span>}</figcaption>
          </figure>
        ))}
      </div>
      <p class="caption" style="margin-top:20px">Every name, task and number on these screens is invented sample data. One vendor name in a sample task title is blurred. The dashboard and its code belong to Doodle Pirates Foundation and are private.</p>
      <div class="btns"><a class="btn solid" href="/ai-builds">More AI builds →</a><a class="btn" href="/contact">Ask me about it</a></div>
    </div></section>

    {broke.length > 0 && (
      <section class="cs-vspace"><div class="wrap cs-grid">
        <div class="sec-head cs-label"><h2>What broke &amp; how I fixed it</h2></div>
        <ol class="numbered">{broke.map((b) => <li><b>{b.title}</b><p>{b.fix}</p></li>)}</ol>
      </div></section>
    )}
    {differently.length > 0 && (
      <section class="cs-vspace"><div class="wrap cs-grid">
        <div class="sec-head cs-label"><h2>What I’d do differently</h2></div>
        <ol class="numbered">{differently.map((d) => <li><p>{d}</p></li>)}</ol>
      </div></section>
    )}
  </article>
</Base>
